{
  "description": "The profit and loss (ACC-07, W2-01 plan, owner answers 2 and 3): one column per period. Income accounts count credits − debits (so returns and discounts are negatives inside revenue), expense accounts debits − credits. The top-level income groups are revenue; the top-level expense group holding the COGS account is the cost of sales, the other expense groups are expenses; asset, liability and equity accounts are left out. A section with one top-level group lists that group's children; with several, the groups themselves and their children. A group's amount is the sum of its children; an account at zero in every period is left out. Gross profit = revenue − cost of sales; net profit = gross profit − expenses. Margins are basis points of revenue, rounded half away from zero, and null when there is no revenue.",
